## Why This Is Asked
Testing for multi-tenant GPU contention and memory fragmentation—particularly after model changes—is critical for real-time inference systems in production environments. Understanding how to isolate GPU resources, detect performance degradation, and maintain SLA guarantees across tenants demonstrates deep infrastructure expertise.

## Key Concepts
- GPU resource isolation using MIG (Multi-Instance GPU) on NVIDIA hardware
- NVML metrics for granular GPU telemetry
- Triton Inference Server integration patterns
- Memory fragmentation versus transient spikes
- Kernel contention and cross-tenant interference detection
- Burst traffic modeling with per-tenant quotas
- Horizontal and vertical autoscaling strategies
- SLO validation and reliability signal collection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo workload generator for multi-tenant GPU testing
function simulateTenantLoad(tenants, ratePerTenant) {
  tenants.forEach(tenant => {
    const requests = generatePoissonRequests(ratePerTenant);
    requests.forEach(req => {
      const batchSize = getRandomBatchSize();
      const startTime = Date.now();
      executeInference(tenant, req, batchSize);
      recordMetrics(tenant, Date.now() - startTime);
    });
  });
}
```

